26. What you've implemented that's actually resume-worthy

At this point PayRoute isn't just:

"I created CRUD APIs using Spring Boot."

You can legitimately say you've implemented:

Java 21
Spring Boot
Spring Security
JWT authentication
PostgreSQL
JPA/Hibernate
BigDecimal monetary calculations
Database transactions
Pessimistic row locking
Optimistic versioning
Idempotency keys
Database unique constraints
Double-entry ledger
Transaction states
Atomic wallet transfers
Concurrency/deadlock awareness

And the most important business invariant is:

For every COMPLETED transfer:


DEBIT amount == CREDIT amount

That is the invariant we'll preserve as PayRoute grows.